# TypeSafe live walkthrough

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:typesafe_api, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Client

The client reads `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` from the environment. If Livebook was launched from the
Dock it will not see your zshrc, so it also falls back to a Livebook secret named
`TYPESAFE_API_KEY` (exposed as `LB_TYPESAFE_API_KEY`).

```elixir
api_key = System.get_env("TYPESAFE_API_KEY") || System.fetch_env!("LB_TYPESAFE_API_KEY")
client = TypeSafe.new(api_key: api_key)
```

## The question set

Three question types, one state. Keys are atoms and round-trip back as atoms.

```elixir
state = "Help! My payouts have been failing for 3 days."

questions = [
  urgent: TypeSafe.noul("Does this convey urgency?"),
  dept:
    TypeSafe.choice("Which team should handle this?",
      billing: "Payments, invoicing, refunds",
      technical: "Bugs, outages, integrations",
      sales: nil
    ),
  anger: TypeSafe.score("How frustrated is the customer?", ["Calm", "Frustrated", "Very angry"])
]
```

## What goes over the wire

`prepare/1` validates and encodes once. The encoded questions are an ordered object so the
API sees them in the order you wrote them.

```elixir
{:ok, prepared} = TypeSafe.SystemOne.prepare(questions)
body = %{"state" => state, "model" => client.model, "questions" => prepared.encoded}

req = TypeSafe.HTTP.build(client, :post, TypeSafe.SystemOne.path(), body)
IO.puts("POST #{client.base_url}#{TypeSafe.SystemOne.path()}")
for {k, v} <- req.headers, k != "authorization", do: IO.puts("#{k}: #{Enum.join(List.wrap(v), ", ")}")
IO.puts("authorization: Bearer sk-***\n")
IO.puts(JSON.encode!(body))
```

## Raw response

The raw HTTP layer returns maps, plus status, headers, request id, and retry count.

```elixir
{:ok, resp} = TypeSafe.HTTP.request(client, :post, TypeSafe.SystemOne.path(), body)
resp
```

## Typed result

`evaluate/3` does all of the above and decodes into typed answer structs.

```elixir
{:ok, result} = TypeSafe.evaluate(client, state, questions)
result.answers
```

```elixir
result.usage
```

## Routing on the answers

```elixir
alias TypeSafe.Answer

cond do
  Answer.yes?(result.answers.urgent) and result.answers.anger.level >= 1 ->
    {:escalate, result.answers.dept.choice}

  true ->
    {:queue, result.answers.dept.choice}
end
```

## Models

```elixir
{:ok, models} = TypeSafe.models(client)
models
```
